            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An implantable apparatus which can be positioned in a body of a patient. The implantable apparatus can comprise a plurality of stimulation zones that are configured to provide tumor treating fields to a target site in one or a plurality of sequences that apply differential stimulation amplitudes and electric field directions relative to the target region in the body, thereby optimizing the treatment efficacy to kill tumor cells in a solid tumor or stray tumor cells in the peripheral area surrounding the tumor.</p>
